# Free-tier profile: the real Gemini engine on an AI Studio project with NO Cloud Billing
# account linked (rehearsals, demos, recording). For a real event use production.env.
# cp examples/env/free-tier.env .env  → fill GEMINI_API_KEY and ADMIN_TOKEN. Never commit .env.
#
# Budget: the free tier allows 15 requests per minute for the text model
# (generate_content_free_tier_requests). Each final caption costs one request per target
# language, progressive translation roughly doubles that, and the auto-glossary adds one
# request per stage start. Two stages with two languages each blow through the 15, and the
# translation fan-out then pauses that language for the time the server asks while the
# audience sees the original text (marker "original"). The keys below keep one stage with
# one language at about 6–8 requests per minute. Live transcription has its own free-tier
# cap on concurrent sessions (a handful), so start only the stages you are watching.
#
# Rule while recording or rehearsing on this profile: watch ONE stage and ONE language at a
# time. Content sent through a free-tier project may be used to improve Google products
# (docs/privacy.md); that is why this profile is not for a real event.
#
# Comments stay on their own lines: after an empty value, "KEY=   # note" makes the note the
# value in the developer path (pydantic-settings), while Docker Compose drops it.
ENGINE=gemini
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# Operator token for /admin: openssl rand -hex 32
ADMIN_TOKEN=
# Translate finals only: about half the requests per minute.
PROGRESSIVE_TRANSLATION=false
# Empty: only languages someone is watching are translated.
ALWAYS_ON_LANGS=
# Saves one text request per stage start.
AUTO_GLOSSARY=false
# One previous segment as context: shorter, cheaper prompts.
TRANSLATE_CONTEXT_SEGMENTS=1
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
